{title: Horse and Rider}
{subtitle: Exodus 15:1–2; 15:20–21}
{key: Cm}
{tempo: 132}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Cm] | ×15

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Miriam took the tambourine
All the women followed her
Dancing on the farther shore
Where the sea [Bb]had closed once [Cm]more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sing to the Lord, [Eb]for he is highly ex[Bb]alted
[Ab]Horse and rider [Eb]he has hurled into the [Bb]sea
[Cm]Sing to the Lord, [Eb]for he is highly ex[Bb]alted
[Ab]Horse and rider [Eb]he has hurled into the [Bb]sea
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] |
| [Cm] | ×16

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The Lord is my strength and my song
He has become my salvation
He is my God and I will praise him
My [Bb]father's God, I [Cm]will exalt him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sing to the Lord, [Eb]for he is highly ex[Bb]alted
[Ab]Horse and rider [Eb]he has hurled into the [Bb]sea
[Cm]Sing to the Lord, [Eb]for he is highly ex[Bb]alted
[Ab]Horse and rider [Eb]he has hurled into the [Bb]sea [Cm]
{end_of_chorus}
